## Chapter 2 Experimental Facilities

The STAR1 experiment is the detector facility at which the data for this thesis were collected. The experiment began taking data in the year 2000 after over a decade of careful design, planning, and assembly. It resides at BNL2, one of ten national laboratories funded by the US Department of Energy. Originally, the STAR experiment was one of four experiments at RHIC3 : STAR, PHENIX4, PHOBOS5, and BRAHMS6. STAR and PHENIX, the two larger experiments, are still actively taking data as of the writing of this thesis.

