### 2.3 Zero Degree Calorimeters

The most basic triggering scheme in a collider experiment is to determine whether or not a collision has occurred. This is referred to as a minimum bias trigger. The ZDC detectors are used, two per RHIC experiment, to help collect minbias triggers. They are hadronic calorimeters which reside 18 m upstream and downstream from an interaction point. They are situated at \(0\,^{\circ}\) with respect to the beam axis, subtending an angle of 2.5 mrad. The purpose of positioning hadronic calorimeters this way is Figure 2.17. The CTB barrel is a series of scintillator tiles that sit in aluminum trays around the circumference of the TPC. Each tray holds two radiators, two light guides, and two PMTs.[49]

