## Appendix C Monte Carlo / Data ComparisonsFigure C.1. The upper left histogram compares the data with loose cuts (top, blue), tight cuts (middle, red) and background (bottom black histogram at the zero level). A peak is visible at \(M_{\pi\pi}=M(K_{s})\). This may be due to photoproduction of the \(\phi\), followed by \(\phi\to K_{s}K_{L}\). Because the Q value of the \(\phi\) decay is so low, most of the \(K_{s}\) still make the \(p_{T}\) cut; the \(K_{L}\) usually vanishes without decaying. The upper right plot compares the data and the Monte Carlo; except for the \(K_{s}\), the agreement is excellent. The lower left plot shows the efficiency; for \(M_{\pi\pi}>550\) MeV/\(c\), the effiency is flat. The last plot shows the \(M_{\pi\pi}\) resolution of about 8.3 MeV [73].

